# SwiftUI conventions

- Swift 6, iOS 17+, iPhone portrait only. `@Observable` view models, `async/await`, no Combine unless required.
- Project is generated by XcodeGen: edit `ios/project.yml`, then run `xcodegen generate`. Never hand-edit `.xcodeproj`.
- Build check after every change: `xcodebuild -scheme IGWrapped -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=<newest installed 6.1-inch non-Pro iPhone>' build`. Do not download a simulator runtime without asking. Name the simulator in the step report.
- Folder ownership: `InstagramShell/` = faithful Instagram chrome. `Features/Cards/` = Wrapped cards. `DesignSystem/` = tokens + components. Do not mix.
- One card = one `View` in `Features/Cards/Personal/<Name>Card.swift`, taking a typed payload. No networking inside cards.
- Lay out cards in a fixed 390 x 844 design space scaled to the device (`DesignCanvas` wrapper) so positions match the PNGs on every iPhone.
- Every interactive element: 44 pt target, `accessibilityLabel`, Reduce Motion branch for animations.
- Add `#Preview` for every card using maya's payload.
- `#if DEBUG` `ReferenceOverlay(image:opacity:)` must be available on every shell screen and card for pixel checks.
